**Prefer `base::EraseIf` (for `base::flat_*` containers) or `std::erase_if` (for
standard containers) over manual iterator-based erase loops.** Cleaner and less
error-prone.

```cpp
// ❌ WRONG - manual erase loop
for (auto it = items.begin(); it != items.end();) {
  if (it->IsExpired()) {
    it = items.erase(it);
  } else {
    ++it;
  }
}

// ✅ CORRECT
base::EraseIf(items, [](const auto& item) { return item.IsExpired(); });
// or for std containers:
std::erase_if(items, [](const auto& item) { return item.IsExpired(); });
```

